WEBVTT

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.430
<i>GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:16.600
The Nue?

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.850
This one seems young and healthy.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:23.140
Too bad for you.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.730
I'm not just any human.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.740
<i>The world you see isn't all there is.</i>

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.700
<i>There are things you can't see.</i>

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.410
<i>See? In the darkness behind you...</i>

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.310
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.310
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.230
<i>Slumbering in bed in the morning</i>

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.230
<i>asa wa nedoko de gu gu gu</i>

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.940
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.940
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.730
<i>Ghosts don't have school</i>

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.730
<i>obakenya gakkou mo</i>

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:16.610
<i>Or tests or anything</i>

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:16.610
<i>shiken mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.410
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.410
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.000
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.000
<i>minna de utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.210
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.210
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:33.090
<i>Sports festivals in the graveyard at night</i>

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:33.090
<i>yoru wa hakaba de undoukai</i>

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.970
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.970
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:42.100
<i>Ghosts don't die</i>

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:42.100
<i>obake wa shinanai</i>

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:45.520
<i>Or get sick or anything</i>

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:45.520
<i>byouki mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:49.980
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:49.980
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.320
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.320
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.280
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.280
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.440
Time just flies.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.700
Kanji will be in
junior high next year, won't he?

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:22.490
What will you do?

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:26.290
I'm thinking of moving.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:29.480
His junior high will be farther away.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.630
Having Yuzo
take him to and from school...

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.710
I couldn't ask Yuzo to do more than
he's done already.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.390
What choice do you have?

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.100
What's that?

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.810
That's a strange cloud.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.200
I gotta pee.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:16.750
Grandpa!

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.660
Thanks, Yuzo.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.640
Sure. How's your grandpa?

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.080
I see...

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:33.750
If you ever need anything,
just say so, Kanji.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:34.980
Okay.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:00.460
Wh-Who... are you?

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.830
I'm GeGeGe no Kitaro.

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:06.850
Are you Kanji?

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:17.730
CHAPTER 50

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:22.650
MESSENGER FROM THE UNDERWORLD
NUE

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:29.160
No letters again today, Dad.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.940
A lot's happened recently.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.540
It'll be like that for a while.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.290
I guess so.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:37.500
Kitaro!

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.950
Let's play, Kitaro!

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:42.210
Catchick...

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:45.200
-Kitaro! Come on, Kitaro!
-Honestly, slow down, Cat-chan.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.800
-Play! Let's play!
-Mana, you're here.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.930
Yeah, I thought I'd play with Cat-chan.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:55.040
She started insisting on going to see you.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.350
Kitaro, let's play!

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.730
Oh all right. Just for a bit.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:03.240
I love Kitaro!

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.240
Kitaro say he play!

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:08.740
Mana-chan play with us, too! Right?

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.830
So cute!

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:14.100
Look at how sweet she is.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:18.330
It would have been nice if she stayed
that sweet when she grew up.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.990
Mana, could you take her on ahead?

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.970
I'll go right after
I clean up Dad's bath bowl.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:28.970
Okay. Cat-chan, let's wait outside.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.560
Be quick, Kitaro!

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.460
Good grief.
Is this how it's going to be for now?

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:42.460
It looks like she's forgotten the past.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:46.970
Once she recovers her <i>yokai</i> power
she'll be back to her old self, right?

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:47.860
Yeah.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:55.250
I thought her soul was annihilated.
I'm surprised you got her back.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.250
Yeah...

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:58.370
Indeed...

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:03.990
<i>Hey, Kitaro! You there?</i>

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:05.550
That's Kagami-Jijii.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.850
It's me. Did you find anything?

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:19.840
<i>No, nothing on
the ones you asked me to look for.</i>

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:22.440
<i>But there's something you should know.</i>

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:23.480
What?

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:28.740
<i>There's been a lot of</i>
yokai<i> going missing recently.</i>

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.860
What do you mean "recently"?

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:35.200
<i>After the Nanashi stuff settled down
of course.</i>

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.560
<i>Hitotsumebo was helping find
information on that thing you asked.</i>

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:42.980
<i>Now I can't reach him anymore.</i>

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:45.420
Then could you look into that, too?

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.050
<i>Got it.</i>

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:50.700
Looking for something?

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:52.340
It's nothing serious.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.660
Ooh! A crow!

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:57.430
Sorry. It looks like there's a letter.

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:05.110
<i>According to Grandpa,</i>

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:11.110
<i>a black cloud suddenly appeared at night
with a monster's shadow in it.</i>

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:14.620
<i>Apparently it had a terrifying roar.</i>

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:19.060
<i>Grandpa and his friend
heard it and fell ill.</i>

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:24.380
<i>I took him to the doctor,
but they have no idea what caused it.</i>

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:29.670
<i>Please. You have to help
my grandpa and everyone.</i>

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.840
Dad, this is...!

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:35.600
Kitaro?

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:37.640
It's a <i>yokai</i> extermination.

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.600
Kitaro, go somewhere?

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.100
Yeah.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.960
Then Cat go, too!

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:46.800
Well, that's...

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:48.070
No!

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:53.280
Cat-chan, you're bothering Kitaro.
Let's house-sit together, okay?

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:55.990
No! Cat go!

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:01.770
I know. Why don't we just
take Catchick with us?

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:02.790
Dad?!

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:06.070
Mt. Osorezan is near where
the letter came from.

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:07.940
Bathing in the hot springs

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:12.800
should restore Catchick's <i>yokai</i> power,
accelerating her regeneration.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:16.890
But, Dad, I'm not sure we'll have time to
visit the hot springs.

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:22.480
Speaking of Mt. Osorezan,
Hanako-san said she was going there.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.060
Hanako-san?

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.810
She's on spring break right now.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:26.710
HOT SPRING GUIDE

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:31.320
That's perfect.
She can look after Catchick.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.070
Will Cat-san return to normal?

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:35.950
Probably.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:38.490
Thank goodness.

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:41.020
She's cute as Cat-chan,

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:45.250
but I prefer Cat-san as her usual Cat-san.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:47.130
Hooray!

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:10.230
This town looks pretty run down, Dad.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:16.110
It looks like the town once thrived
on a mine or something.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:19.220
Hey, Kitaro-san!

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:20.520
Rollo Cloth.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:21.770
What is it?

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:24.120
Got a message for ya from Hanako-san.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:27.560
Something's come up and I'll be late.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:28.750
I'm sorry.

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:30.150
I see.

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:35.280
Oh well. Let's first meet with
the boy who sent the letter.

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:38.080
Catchick, can you behave yourself?

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:38.890
Sure!

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:44.670
I'm GeGeGe no Kitaro.

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:46.890
Are you Kanji?

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.060
Y-Yes.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:52.900
I'm Catchick!

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.930
Could you tell me what--

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:59.160
Kitaro! I'm hungry!

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.240
Huh?

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:04.100
Sorry, Catchick. Can you wait a little?

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:06.790
No! I'm hungry!

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.960
Food! Food!

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:10.290
Excuse me.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:12.540
If you'd like...

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.670
Go on. Eat up.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.970
Look yummy!

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.810
You're a good cook.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:30.230
Well, it's only Grandpa and me
living here.

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:34.190
There aren't any stores nearby,
so we have to cook for ourselves.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:36.320
I see. How admirable.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:40.910
It's nothing special.
This is normal for me.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:44.540
Besides, I love this town.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:50.870
But it's a long way to
the bigger town that has a doctor.

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:52.980
That worries me.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.860
Can we speak to your grandfather?

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:56.760
Yes.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.040
I wanted him hospitalized,

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:09.230
but he said, "there's no point in staying
if they can't cure me," and came home.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:13.270
Grandpa, Kitaro-san's here.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.920
He wants to talk.

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:18.300
Kanji! Want more!

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:22.360
-Kanji-kun, could you look after Catchick?
-Kanji! Kanji!

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.950
-Okay.
-Hurry! Hurry!

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:27.450
Excuse me.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:36.210
Forgive my appearance.

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:38.610
It's all right.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:42.510
You heard a terrifying voice from
a black cloud at night?

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:49.080
Y-Yes. It was
a truly, truly terrifying roar.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:53.840
It was like nothing of this world.
Like something being strangled...

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:57.150
It was a voice that chilled me to my soul.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:00.650
And ever since you heard that voice...

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.760
Well, just look at me.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:08.020
It happened to old Yamamura,
who was with me, too.

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:09.540
And there are others.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:14.880
I heard Genzo and Masaharu Ono
were kidnapped.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:16.110
Dad...

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:18.880
It seems to all add up.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:22.510
Did you get something from that?

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:27.010
Yes. This seems to be the doing of a <i>yokai</i>
called the Nue.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:28.760
The Nue?

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:31.830
He appears in The Tale of the Heike.

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:37.840
A monkey's face, a <i>tanuki</i>'s body,
a tiger's legs, and a snake for a tail.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:44.030
His roar is utterly terrifying,
causing those who hear it to fall ill.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.700
And the Nue

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:54.670
is one of the evil <i>yokai</i> known as
The Four Treasonous Generals.

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:58.670
NUE

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:03.170
CATCHICK

00:13:01.190 --> 00:13:02.070
-<i>"I was sleeping."</i>
-<i>"Sorry."</i>

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:03.070
<i>"Smack!"</i>

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:13.810
Here we go.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:17.650
Cat do it too!

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:22.990
Don't burn yourself.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:28.620
Kitaro-san, do ya really think
ya can lure the Nue out with this?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.140
Probably.

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:34.750
I had Kanji-kun check the dates
when each person was attacked.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.500
It turns out...

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:39.320
there was one common factor.

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:40.380
The darkness.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:41.900
Darkness?

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:47.370
On the attack days, the moon was either
hidden by clouds, or there was a new moon.

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:49.640
And tonight happens to be a new moon.

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:53.330
Then why light these lanterns?

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:57.390
If he likes the dark,
wouldn't lightin' these lanterns be bad?

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:01.880
There's probably
one more condition to the attacks.

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:06.640
Kanji-kun, you were in the same house
when your grandfather was attacked.

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:09.390
But you never fell ill.

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:10.370
How come?

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:13.240
Because I was asleep.

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.690
Exactly.

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:19.060
That means the Nue's voice
has no effect on sleeping people.

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:20.460
Meaning...

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:21.900
I get it!

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:27.220
It targets homes with lights on
where people are still awake!

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:32.950
Pretty!

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:33.870
Yeah.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:36.990
Okay. We're all set.

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:38.850
Leave the rest to us.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:41.730
I should go home?

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:44.230
Yeah. It's dangerous.

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:50.110
Why do you help us when it's dangerous,
Kitaro-san?

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:58.250
Consider it repaying a debt to
someone who helped me a long time ago.

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:00.940
However...

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:05.250
this time, that's not the only reason
I'm facing the Nue.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:07.260
Kitaro-san?

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:10.160
You better get home, Kanji-kun.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:11.450
Catchick.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:13.660
Go back with Kanji-kun.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:15.760
No! I stay with Kitaro!

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:18.680
No. It's dangerous.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:19.890
Got it?

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:28.240
It's almost midnight.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:33.760
There's a cloud!

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:37.270
It shouldn't work on us,
but you never know.

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.950
Keep your ears well covered.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:40.350
Gotcha!

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:42.460
These are my ears. Didn't ya know?

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:43.480
Dad!

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:44.340
Right!

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:54.510
<i>A person?!</i>

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:56.760
<i>We're too late!</i>

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:06.690
Oh no!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.220
Rollo Cloth, we're following!

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:16.740
Cotton copies!

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:22.580
Are Kitaro-san and the others okay?

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:26.750
At least Cat-chan went to sleep
without a fuss.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:35.430
Kitaro! Where are you?

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:44.730
That's...

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:49.230
Those were probably apartments
for workers in the mine.

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:53.240
The people left and they were abandoned.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:57.030
Apparently it costs a lot
to tear them down.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:04.980
This one seems young and healthy.

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:08.000
This should last me a while.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:20.640
So you weakened and kidnapped people
so you could drain their life force.

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.520
You... Are you...?

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:30.980
Kitaro? Dammit!

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.440
Remote Controlled Geta!

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:34.700
A-whoops!

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:36.740
Hair Needles!

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:38.780
Ow, ow, ow!

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:42.040
Spirit Hair Chanchanko!

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:47.370
Give it up, Nue!

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:49.170
W-Wait!

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:51.550
I'm not the Nue!

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.840
MUJINA

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.970
You're... the Mujina?!

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:00.580
That's right.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:02.810
Huh?! Ya were fakin'?

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:05.020
Gimme a break!

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:08.630
I was told to disguise myself as the Nue!

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:11.190
Otherwise I'd be pulverized!

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:14.570
That thrush is his servant!

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:21.080
What do we do, Kitaro?
We didn't expect a fake.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:23.990
Oh! Found you!

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:27.790
No! No!

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:30.040
Let her go!

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:33.800
Come on, Kitaro. You've gotta let me go.

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:38.120
I'll let the girl go if you do.

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:40.800
-Come on!
-No!

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:44.060
Let her go, <i>yokai</i>.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:51.800
Wh-Why...?

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:54.440
You were unconscious from my voice.

00:18:59.030 --> 00:18:59.950
It's these.

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:02.570
Simple earplugs couldn't protect...

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:06.440
These are the latest
noise cancelling earphones.

00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:10.400
They can shut out nearly 100%
of the surrounding noises.

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:15.210
Don't make me repeat myself.
Let that girl go!

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:17.200
Shut up!

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:20.090
I don't take orders from humans!

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:22.830
Too bad for you.

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:25.100
I'm not just any human.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:32.100
<i>ONI</i>

00:19:32.860 --> 00:19:35.400
Summon <i>kijin</i>!

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:47.450
Wh...

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:52.860
Those are... arms of the <i>kijin</i>?!

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:54.500
That spell! It can't be...!

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:00.920
I thought it was human,
but it's just a <i>yokai</i>.

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:05.260
Hardly worth saving.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:07.290
Spill it.

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:10.020
Where's the real Nue?

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:14.920
These are arms of the <i>kijin</i>.

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:18.610
They can crush your head
like it's nothing.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:22.430
He's in Tokyo!

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:25.760
He had me cause a commotion
way up in the Tohoku region

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:29.580
so he could claim the capital
while everyone was focused here!

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:33.330
A diversion. That sneaky little...

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:36.090
I told you! Now let me go!

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:37.960
No.

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:42.720
You're going to help feed my power now.

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:52.480
<i>On!</i>

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.310
MUJINA

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:01.300
He absorbed a <i>yokai</i>'s life?!

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:04.240
It really is a Kidoshu spell.

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:06.950
Kidoshu?

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:10.160
Kitaro!

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:15.080
That <i>yokai</i> didn't intend to fight anymore.

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:17.170
You didn't have to go that far.

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:19.800
It attacked humans.

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:22.050
He was being ordered to.

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:25.550
Even so, that doesn't change its crime.

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:30.430
Every <i>yokai</i> that would harm humans
is a pest that must be hunted down.

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:33.060
Who are you?

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:37.310
Rei Isurugi of the Kidoshu.

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:39.550
The Nue is mine.

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:41.720
I'll defeat any in my way.

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:46.320
Even you, GeGeGe no Kitaro.

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:56.400
So he's appeared.

00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:58.830
GeGeGe no Kitaro.

00:23:01.730 --> 00:23:04.610
<i>The Nue runs wild
and the city is in chaos.</i>

00:23:04.610 --> 00:23:07.860
<i>Dad, just what is Rei Isurugi after?</i>

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:10.530
<i>Next time on GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:12.870
<i>"Enma-Daio's Secret Bargain"</i>

00:23:12.870 --> 00:23:15.450
<i>The door to the unseen world opens...</i>
